# CQ-17 · quality-inventory
#
# Question: Which Quality dimensions does the corpus use, how many Qualities
#           carry each, and in how many documents?
# Persona:  P2 — scene-data annotator / ML researcher. The dimension registry is
#           closed under the VSO namespace (§5.5.1); the coverage question is
#           which of the twenty-one registered axes has ever been written.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.5 (`vso:Quality`); §5.5.1 (the registry); §2 C2/C7
# Form:     SELECT — one row per dimension in use
# Note:     The bearer edge is `vso:hasQuality|vso:hasInvariant`, a SPARQL 1.1
#           property alternative, because a Persona's invariants are Qualities
#           on the other edge (§5.3.4) and an inventory that counted only one of
#           the two would under-report the appearance axes. The Quality node
#           itself is deliberately not projected: `examples/throne_room.ttl`
#           writes its Qualities as blank nodes, whose labels are minted per
#           parse and cannot be frozen.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?dimension (COUNT(*) AS ?qualities) (COUNT(DISTINCT ?doc) AS ?documents)
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?bearer  vso:hasQuality|vso:hasInvariant ?quality .
    ?quality vso:dimension ?dimension .
  }
}
GROUP BY ?dimension
ORDER BY ?dimension
